# SYNTHESISED to model a structured-output (terraform.ui JSON) HCP Terraform raw run log. Values are invented; no line here is from a real run. The object structure -- including hook.resource.addr being a string alongside module, resource, implied_provider, resource_type, resource_name and resource_key, and the apply_start/apply_complete pair with action:"read" for a refresh -- was confirmed against a real run by a user who could not share the log itself. The second resource's apply_start/apply_progress/apply_errored sequence models a failed create: that elapsed_seconds is a float64, that apply_progress carries a partial "still working" elapsed_seconds which must never be treated as a completion, and that apply_errored carries a real total elapsed_seconds, are facts checked against the hashicorp/terraform source (internal/command/views/json/hook.go and message_types.go), not against a real run. NOTE: the 1.2 and 2.5 elapsed_seconds values here are deliberately unrealistic. Terraform rounds both the start and the end of a resource's timing to the nearest second before subtracting them (internal/command/views/hook_json.go), so a real log's elapsed_seconds is always a whole number -- confirmed across 503 spans in two real HCP runs. The fractional values are kept only to exercise float64 parsing and the sub-second duration formatting that RPC-tier spans do produce.
